$ jailops explain
CODE                    EXIT   CAUSE                                                                                                                             FIX
invalid                 2      The server rejected the request: a field is missing, malformed or out of range.                                                   Read the message, correct the named field and retry; 'jailops firewall validate' checks rules offline.
not_found               4      The named object does not exist on this host (objects of jails and snapshots are per host).                                       List the kind to see the names, check --host and --remote, and check the spelling.
already_exists          5      An object of that kind and name already exists.                                                                                   Pick another name, or edit the existing object.
conflict                5      The object changed on the server after you read it (stale generation, HTTP 412).                                                  Read it again and repeat the change; 'jailops <kind> edit' does this for you.
unauthorized            3      The server did not accept your credential: no token, an expired or revoked token, or an unknown certificate.                      Check the token with 'jailops remote list' and 'jailops doctor'; create a new token on the server if needed.
forbidden               3      Your credential is valid but its role does not allow this action.                                                                 Ask an administrator for a token with a higher role (operator for lifecycle, admin for configuration).
unsupported             6      The server does not implement this feature, or a missing API extension.                                                           Upgrade the server, or use a different command; 'jailops server info' lists the extensions.
busy                    5      Another operation holds a lock on the resource, or the server is temporarily overloaded.                                          Wait for the running operation ('jailops op list') and retry.
internal                7      The server failed in a way the client cannot fix.                                                                                 Retry once, then report the request id shown with the error and check the server log.
quota_exceeded          5      Creating or growing this object would take the project over one of its quotas (jails, CPU, memory, PIDs, addresses or storage).   See the usage with 'jailops project show NAME', free something up, or ask a global admin to raise the quota with 'jailops project set NAME --max-...'.
ip_conflict             5      The requested address is already used by another jail or is outside the network range.                                            Use 'auto' or another address; 'jailops network leases NAME' shows what is taken.
pool_exhausted          5      The network has no free addresses left in its range.                                                                              Widen the range of the network or remove unused jails.
image_in_use            5      A jail still uses this image or image generation.                                                                                 Upgrade or delete the jails listed in the message, then retry.
data_loss_unconfirmed   2      The operation would discard data and was sent without confirmation.                                                               Check what would be lost (the CLI shows the bytes written) and confirm by typing the jail name or with --confirm-data-loss.
version_skew            6      The client, hub and host run API versions too far apart for this call.                                                            Upgrade the older side; 'jailops server info' shows both versions.
not_leader              7      This node is not the cluster leader and cannot accept the change.                                                                 Retry against the leader named in the error detail, or through the hub.
no_quorum               7      The cluster has lost its quorum and cannot commit changes.                                                                        Restore enough nodes to form a majority; reads keep working.
unverified_platform     6      The feature needs FreeBSD or a kernel facility that this host does not provide or that was never proven there.                    Run the host on FreeBSD 15.1 or later with the facility enabled; see the unverified list in the documentation.
zfs_incompatible        6      The ZFS pool or dataset lacks a feature the operation needs.                                                                      Upgrade the pool features ('zpool upgrade') on both ends of the transfer.
chain_broken            5      A backup chain has a missing or corrupt link, so later snapshots cannot be restored from it.                                      Run 'jailops backup verify' and take a new full backup.
merge_conflict          5      The /etc merge during an upgrade needs a human; the jail stays on the old generation.                                             Resolve the listed files in the jail, then run 'jailops jail upgrade' again.
rate_limited            3      Too many failed authentication attempts from this source.                                                                         Wait a few minutes and retry with the correct credential.
key_not_escrowed        2      A raw backup was refused because its key has no recoverable escrow.                                                               Escrow the backup key first, then repeat the backup.
maintenance             5      The backup node is read-only or offline for maintenance.                                                                          Retry later; 'jailops backup target list' shows which target is affected.
missing_chunks          5      A backup commit refers to chunks the repository does not have.                                                                    Run the backup again so the missing chunks are uploaded; this is normal after an interrupted run.
lease_expired           5      The backup session timed out or was closed by the node before it finished.                                                        Run the backup again; a slow link may need a longer session on the node.
not_managed             3      JailOps does not manage this part of the host: jailopsd.yaml or priv.conf does not enable the module.                             Add the lines the hint names and restart both services, or change the host by hand (docs/appliance.md).
plaintext_denied        2      A backup node target would receive unencrypted data and the policy does not allow plaintext.                                      Enable backup encryption, or set allow_plaintext on the target if that is intended.

$ jailops explain data_loss_unconfirmed
data_loss_unconfirmed

Cause:  The operation would discard data and was sent without confirmation.
Fix:    Check what would be lost (the CLI shows the bytes written) and confirm by typing the jail name or with --confirm-data-loss.
HTTP:   400
Exit:   2

$ jailops explain not_found -o json
{
  "code": "not_found",
  "cause": "The named object does not exist on this host (objects of jails and snapshots are per host).",
  "fix": "List the kind to see the names, check --host and --remote, and check the spelling."
}

$ jailops explain no_such_code
! not_found: unknown error code "no_such_code"
! hint: run 'jailops explain' for the list of codes
[exit 4]

